  "details": "Reposting this in OB board to make sure this doesn't get forgotten. \n\nThere's already multiple requests for the same thing: \n\n* https://feedback.vrchat.com/feature-requests/p/images-store-exifiptc-metadata-for-images-taken \n\n* https://feedback.vrchat.com/feature-requests/p/adding-world-name-player-in-frame-metadata-to-screenshot \n\n* https://feedback.vrchat.com/feature-requests/p/photos-saved-by-virtual-camera-could-contain-some-metadata-with-the-names-of-the\n\nWith prints already doing this, there's no real reason not to embed the same metadata in locally saved pictures, including high-resolution ones. This would allow this data to also be retained if someone uploads a locally taken picture later as a print.",
